Model Improvement Lab v3.0.0

The orchestration, training utilities and capture tools in this package are
provided under Apache License 2.0. No target weights or draft weights are included.

The model implementation in source/ derives from DFlash by Z Lab and remains
subject to the MIT license in licenses/DFlash-MIT.txt, including the extracted
layer, sampling and model utility modules.
Upstream: https://github.com/z-lab/dflash

The capture tools use APIs from the compatible llama.cpp fork. That runtime is
not bundled. Its source and license must be obtained separately.
Runtime source: https://github.com/mistrjirka/llama.cpp

The EAGLE-3 companion patches modify SpecForge and llama.cpp. See
licenses/SpecForge-MIT.txt and licenses/llama.cpp-MIT.txt for their notices.
The llama.cpp patch includes Volta work from the following public commits:
https://github.com/anyei/llamacpp-v100/commit/d6c02899a83c175fc3e56f3b07c6da0f4b6e5ee3
https://github.com/mistrjirka/llama.cpp/commit/67fb99911b2d80845276e6ec0e048a7711b052a6
https://github.com/mistrjirka/llama.cpp/commit/28f085911f94f56a91485bdcb3c2dcfb3acaa87f

Public dataset references are examples authorized for inclusion. Dataset files
are not bundled. Follow the source notices and terms of each downloaded dataset.

No private training records, checkpoints, prompts, server configuration,
credentials or measured results are distributed with this package.

Downloaded companion checkpoints retain their upstream licenses. Qwen3.5,
Qwen3-ASR and CLAP recipes reference Apache-2.0 models; Music Flamingo uses
NVIDIA OneWay Noncommercial terms, restricted to academic, non-commercial use.
No companion model weights are distributed in this source repository.
